Package: khervefitting
Version: @VERSION@
Section: science
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Depends: libgtk-3-0 | libgtk-3-0t64, libglib2.0-0 | libglib2.0-0t64, libsm6, libxtst6, libxxf86vm1, libgl1, libnotify4, librsvg2-common, fonts-liberation, xdg-utils
Recommends: libwebkit2gtk-4.1-0 | libwebkit2gtk-4.0-37, libasound2 | libasound2t64, fonts-dejavu-core
Maintainer: Gwilherm Kerherve <gwilherm.kerherve@gmail.com>
Homepage: https://github.com/KherveFitting/KherveFitting
Description: XPS peak fitting and analysis software
 KherveFitting is an application for processing X-ray photoelectron
 spectroscopy (XPS) data. It reads the common instrument formats (VAMAS,
 Kratos, PHI, Thermo Avantage and plain text exports), performs background
 subtraction and peak fitting with a range of line shapes, and exports the
 results as Excel workbooks, plots and reports.
 .
 This package bundles the Python runtime and every Python dependency. It uses
 the system GTK so that it follows the desktop's own theme, which is why the
 GTK libraries are listed as dependencies.
